WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.190
I’m really sorry, everyone.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.110
To think that that woman had bought up all
of the super tuna to sabotage you guys...

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.320
Don’t worry about it.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.370
It’s not like it’s your fault.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:15.870
That’s right.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.870
In fact, we think that you’re a good guy.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.830
After all, you’re doing something
that feels so very good...

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.590
Oh my God, guys...

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.560
Why is everyone naked in my office?

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.420
What in the world is...?

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.710
Tsubodzuka wanted to make up for Yukino’s having bought out all of the tuna

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.310
by giving us all acupuncture.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.310
Would you like to join us, Madam President?
It feels real good.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.740
I’ll pass.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.740
You’re so impure, Kawachi.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.320
Yeah, what a perverted baldy.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.040
Yeah, but Tsubodzuka...

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:56.910
Yes?

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.540
Since we’re all friends now,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.660
it’s gonna be kinda hard to fight it out
with you in the next match.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.460
If it’s just that, don’t worry...

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.180
I’ve quit being a member of CMAP.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:10.680
Huh?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.140
By quit, do you mean that you’ve retired?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.680
Well, I remembered something after watching you guys.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.180
I remembered that you can’t make truly
delicious food if you’re not having fun making it.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.070
But...

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.810
In CMAP, everybody is a rival.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.530
We only pretend to get along on television.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.330
We’re in no state to be enjoying cooking.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.200
That is why I quit.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.410
Oh, I see...

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:43.750
In that case, we don’t have to hold back on crushing CMAP.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:45.830
But, you can’t relax yet.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.840
If it’s just about skill, they are true professionals.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.340
It won’t be good to let down your guard.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.470
We’re professionals at baking, too,

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.180
so we have no complaints about our opponents.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.560
Let’s do this.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.930
Let’s go!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.270
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.190
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.440
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.910
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:20.080
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.590
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:34.550
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:40.720
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:55.820
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:04.410
probably helped me notice that

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:10.290
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:19.180
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.550
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:31.690
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:37.480
that white sky with my colors.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:44.490
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.870
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.970
Ooo, mango!!

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.520
CMAP’s big counterattack!

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.010
Jungle Office

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.650
I see...

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.270
Kaname Hiroshi

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:15.020
It looks like the enemy was strong enough to take down Tsubodzuka-kun...

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.860
So, you want all of us to fight in the next match.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.030
Am I right?

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:23.780
That’s right.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.030
Geez, how stupid.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.080
Chimatsuri Gou
Geez, how stupid.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.250
Why do the three of us have to get together to fight small fry like that?
Chimatsuri Gou

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:30.490
I’m going to turn it down as well.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.500
Narumi Shizoto
I’m going to turn it down as well.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.460
I mean, if the three of us are going to participate,
Narumi Shizoto

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.750
there’d be two incompetent people I’d be
better off without as they’d just pull me down.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.680
What was that?!

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.760
Who you calling an incompetent person you’re
better off without ’cause he’s pulling you down?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.770
You perverted narcissist!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.930
Whoa, whoa.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.600
These old-fashioned thugs from the
boonies sure are short-tempered.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.600
You little...

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.100
You guys are low-class, as always.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.360
Don’t you be starting, too.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.740
It looks like...

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.160
You guys get along real well.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.460
That’s one way of putting it.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:11.750
In reality, surviving in CMAP is
much harder than people imagine.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.580
It’s an everyday occurrence for
someone to be dragging you down.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.500
Hey, stop right there, four-eyes.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.090
Isn’t it always <i>you</i> who’s dragging us down?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:19.890
Huh?

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.680
It’s you who’s spreading all those
ridiculous scandals, isn’t it?!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.010
You?!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:25.840
How stupid.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.680
There isn’t any advantage for me
in doing something like that.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.770
Shut up, you bastard!

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:32.390
Spill it.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.520
Spill it already, will ya?

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.060
I... I-I’m against violence!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.810
I can’t take this anymore.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.070
Will the two of you just die already?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.070
Spill it! Spill it! Spill it! Spill it! Spill it! Spill it!

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.780
These guys are ridiculous.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.780
Is it really time to be doing this?

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.210
Wh-Who’s the old dude?

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.130
It’s the Director of St. Pierre, Kirisaki.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.330
Look at that.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.590
Retirement!?
Tsubodzuka Takumi!
CMAP collapses
Crisis!!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:08.140
It makes no difference to me whether
scum like that loses or retires.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.650
However, we can’t be saying that.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.690
With him having lost, people will
think that in reality, CMAP is weak.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:18.150
Once such rumors spread,
the number of our jobs will decrease,

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.820
and our popularity will take a dive.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.560
Exactly.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.610
Right now, what you guys need most is a complete victory.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.790
To defeat the enemy completely and mercilessly, by working together.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.330
Don’t you think so?

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.500
Fine.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.640
But, there’s no way I’m taking orders from anyone.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.590
How exactly do you want the three of us
to get along at this point in time?

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.050
There’s no need for you to get along!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.420
When you make bread using a specialty ingredient,

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.520
you can break up the tasks
into at least three:

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:58.930
choosing the ingredients, preparing the
ingredients, and making the bread.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.280
All you need to do is divide
these tasks amongst yourselves,

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.440
and promise not to interfere with each other.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.110
I see...

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.450
It’s true that this way, we can work
separately without any problems.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.910
It’s a wonderful idea.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.460
But, choosing the ingredients merely means
you have to judge quality, right?

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.210
How about I do that?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.090
Huh? Is that okay with you?

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:26.670
In exchange, you can’t use any
ingredients but the ones I choose.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.550
In other words,

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.430
in the end, it will be me who
decides what bread you’ll make.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.150
That’s why you...

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.110
Whatever.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.690
What about you?

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.320
You want to prepare the ingredients, or make the bread?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.570
Isn’t that obvious?

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.690
This is a bread battle, after all,
so I choose to make the bread.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:50.320
No matter what specialty items you choose
and how you prepare them...

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.700
I’ll knead you a perfect bread...

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.200
with this Flame Arm of mine!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:10.460
And now, we’ll open the panel chosen by
the loser from the last round, St. Pierre!

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.510
Saito

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:17.070
The match for the third round will be held in Saito.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.010
Saito?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:19.980
Saito refers to the city of Saito in Miyazaki prefecture.
Saito

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:22.650
Saito refers to the city of Saito in Miyazaki prefecture.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:27.280
It is famous for the Saito plains,
which house many ancient tombs.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.110
You should also try making a great bread that, like the tombs,

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.030
will be talked about
for generations to come.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:33.450
Saito...

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.630
What are its specialty products?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.000
Whoa.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:41.560
City of Saito, Miyazaki Prefecture

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.400
Note: Haniwa (<b>埴輪): Unglazed earthen objects made in ancient Japan.
What a huge haniwa!
City of Saito, Miyazaki Prefecture</b>

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:46.280
Just as you’d expect of Saito,
the city of ancient tombs...
City of Saito, Miyazaki Prefecture

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.000
But, we can’t really make a bread out of haniwa...
City of Saito, Miyazaki Prefecture

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.470
But, we can’t really make a bread out of haniwa...

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:52.510
The specialty product of this place is ripe mango.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.020
Ripe...

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.020
Mangoes?

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:57.930
These perfectly ripe mangoes are grown in greenhouses.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.940
Just before the plant begins
to fruit, it is wrapped in nets.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.600
Then, you wait for the fruit to ripen
completely and fall off on its own.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.520
So, these mangoes are cultivated
using this special technique.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.020
It’s a high-quality fruit whose
elegant aroma and rich sweetness

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:14.290
have led to it being called the Queen of Fruit.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.780
They’re selling it wholesale over there.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.460
One look is worth a hundred words.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.460
So, let’s go take a look.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:23.290
Okay!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:23.880
<b>3 pieces</b>

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.080
Whoa!
<b>3 pieces</b>

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.290
7000 yen for just three pieces?!
<b>3 pieces</b>

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.840
The Miyazaki prefecture competes for first
or second place in the entire country

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.430
for the number of good weather days in a single year,

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:38.350
so the fruit cultivated here are high in sugar
content and are of extremely high quality.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.520
Thus, while other prefectures also
produce perfectly ripe mangoes,

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.770
the ones sold here are priced higher.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.860
Well, it’s true that...

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:50.020
Would you like to try some?

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.940
Is that okay, Granny?

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.450
Yep. Go ahead.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.410
Whoa.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.700
These look really delicious.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.530
I’ll help myself then.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.330
Ooo, mango!

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.020
C... Could this be...

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.360
a reaction to the ripe mango?

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.520
A kanchou mango?!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:37.030
Ooo, mango!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.740
Kawachi... That’s called a mambo, not a mango.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.420
What in the world was I...?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.830
I don’t believe this.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.800
There’s an idiot having a reaction in this kind of place.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:52.670
Geez.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.940
If you’re going to have a reaction with just the ingredients,

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.760
there isn’t a need to make bread, is there?

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.510
Say, Kaname...

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.430
Did Tsubodzuka really lose to these idiots?

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.010
Well, so it seems.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.140
God, that Tsubodzuka...

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.520
He really is scum.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.480
Kinda want him to die, right?

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:14.230
Yeah, and we don’t even know what he means when he uses those foreign words...

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.740
Hey, you assholes!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.620
I really can’t appreciate someone
who makes fun of a former companion.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.960
Companion?

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:27.830
What an idiot.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.340
You’re standing up for that kinda guy?

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.710
Kinda want him to die, right?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.750
I see... Is that what it was?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:40.140
Tsubodzuka-kun must have lost
on purpose to make us look bad.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.470
I see...

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:45.430
That’s why they’re standing up for that kinda guy.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.100
That little piece of shit...

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.310
For real?

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.070
Now I kinda want Tsubodzuka to die twice over.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.360
Hey, cut the crap, or...

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.740
Unforgivable...
Hey, cut the crap, or...

00:11:55.530 --> 00:12:00.530
Someone like you can’t compare to Tsubodzuka.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.950
I’m going to crush people like you with my <i>Japan</i>!

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.720
“I’m going to crush people like you with my <i>Japan</i>,” eh?

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.100
I’m so mad...

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.180
That damn brat.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:27.890
Yeah, I really want to kinda kill them all.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:32.390
Yeah, the very use of a pun like <i>Japan</i> is meaningless.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.980
So, what’re we gonna do, Kaname?

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.150
You’re the one choosing ingredients, right?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.400
Of course.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.700
Take a look.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.110
Is this...

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:42.650
Mango curry?!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.120
Exactly.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.580
To know from only giving the recipe a single glance...

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:47.620
you guys really are impressive.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:53.130
To create high-quality curry with a
deep flavor, people often use mangoes.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:57.170
But, you’re probably never heard of a
luxury curry made of ripe mango, correct?

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:01.130
If we fill bread with this, we can
present it as a specialty product of Saito.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.260
This is bad...

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.890
Just thinking of it makes me drool.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:06.060
Not too bad.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.890
You know... you’re allowed to live
for another five years, I guess.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:12.690
Well, since there are no complaints about the menu,

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.770
let’s make the ultimate mango curry bread,

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.570
and let’s educate them on how very harsh, severe and...

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:20.120
how spicy life can be.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:21.200
Yep.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.110
Let’s kinda have them die on us.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.660
Pantasia
Lodgings
Nakisou

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:33.120
The guesthouse in Ooma was “about to die,”
and the guesthouse here is “about to cry,” eh?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:36.710
If it’s going to be like this every time,
then I really might cry.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.090
We have to keep our belts tight,

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.920
so please put up with this amount of dirt.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.630
It’s not really the dirt...

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.400
I mean, while it may be a city of ancient tombs,

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.310
there’s just these weird creepy haniwas all around us.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.390
So, what do you want to do?

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:53.730
All three of them are pretty skilled.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.890
If we don’t have an idea that won’t lose to them...

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:59.360
If we were to process ripe mangoes
and put them in bread,

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.530
then pudding, jelly, jam...

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.400
With something like that, can we win against them?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.900
No, processing them is no good.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.160
This is something that should
be eaten in its original state.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.660
In its original state?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.660
Yeah...

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:17.080
It’s a fruit that could get such an
amazing reaction out of Kawachi.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.420
So, it’s certain that it will be
more delicious if we don’t process it.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:22.630
But...

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.090
Bread is essentially something that you bake or fry.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.680
If you put the fruit in just like that,
it’ll get cooked with the bread.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.640
But, it’s not impossible.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.310
What was that?!

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:37.440
I hope you’re not thinking of just adding
the mango to bread after baking it, right?

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:39.150
If we do something like that...

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:40.560
Kuro-yan is sure to...

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.820
This is not mango-bread!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.950
This is mango and bread!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:48.030
He’ll say something like that,
and we’ll lose in one fell swoop.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.820
Geez...

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.080
I wouldn’t do something stupid like that.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.660
Then, what are you going to do?

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.210
Freeze it.

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.660
Just before we bake it, we just have to freeze it a little.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:57.910
Freeze it?

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:02.210
Fortunately, mango is quite resilient
against being frozen and thawed.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:04.880
So, it shouldn’t be much of a problem.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.010
Yeah.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.380
I see.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.970
Waffle dough would go well with bread.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.970
So, shall we try making it?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:13.680
Yeah...

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.820
Yep, let’s try it!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:17.930
All right.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.940
All done.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.440
Its appearance is so-so, I guess.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.900
The question is the taste.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.160
It doesn’t quite feel right.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.120
I wonder what the problem is...

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.500
There are probably three big problems.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.250
Firstly, since it has been baked after being frozen,

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.880
while it is subtle, some of it has turned liquid,
affecting the texture of the waffle negatively.

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:48.380
Secondly, the artificial sweetness of the waffle

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.130
does not complement the natural
sweetness of the mango at all.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.110
And thirdly...

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.860
and this is the biggest problem of all...

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.390
It’s really, really bloody hard to eat!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.890
You said it.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:05.900
Say, Azuma...

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.400
Don’t you think it’s a good idea
to look for another way?

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.650
Regarding the liquification of the fruit...

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:18.160
We just have to use a shock freezer
instead of a regular one.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.670
In other words, by flash-freezing the mango,

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:25.500
you can overcome the problem caused
when the fruit’s water content freezes,

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:30.170
causing the cells to expand and lyse, leading to liquification during the thaw cycle.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.640
But the other two problems are a little...

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.180
Let’s give up, Azuma.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.390
Okay?

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.230
Let’s give up.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:45.950
It’s you!

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.610
That’s it! It’s you!

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.570
It has to be you!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:54.110
Kanmuri, can you really fix the first problem?

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.290
Uh, yeah, I guess.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.870
Then, it’s decided.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.710
We’ll crush them with this haniwa...

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.880
With Haniwa-<i>Japan</i>.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.330
W-With the haniwa?!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:10.630
Kawachi, can you get other fruit that can be
obtained in the Miyazaki prefecture tomorrow?

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.550
Not a problem, but what are you planning to do?

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.840
Isn’t it obvious?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:16.350
We’ll mix them all up and add them to the dough.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:17.770
I see!

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.930
If it’s dough that’s been sweetened with fruit kneaded in,

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.100
then it should be compatible with the
natural flavor of the mango as well.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.650
So, you mean...

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:24.360
In other words,

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:26.020
we can fix the second problem

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.510
of the artificial sweetness of the waffle not being compatible

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:30.280
with the natural sweetness of the mango.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.610
Yep, that’s right.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.910
B... But, the biggest weakness...

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.200
What are we going to do about
it being bloody hard to eat?

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.950
It’s all right.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.160
That problem will be all solved by this haniwa.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:41.880
The day of the 2nd match
That problem will be all solved by this haniwa.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.000
The day of the 2nd match

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.460
It’s really hot.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.420
As expected of the Miyazaki prefecture,

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.130
which competes over first and second place
for the number of days with good weather.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:53.750
Yeah.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.600
At this rate, we could just faint
from the heat during the match.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:58.970
But...

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.970
our opponents have to face the same problem.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.190
What’s with him?

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:04.900
It’s hot...
What’s with him?

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:05.610
It’s so hot, yet he isn’t even breaking a sweat at all.
It’s hot...

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.980
It’s so hot, yet he isn’t even breaking a sweat at all.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.480
What’s wrong, Kanmuri?

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.990
That Chimatsuri guy isn’t sweating at...

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:14.700
Sweat?

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:20.490
Well then, we will now begin
Yakitate!! 9’s third match here at Saito.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.490
Both teams... Begin!

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:32.760
Manager...

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:33.970
This fragrance...

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:35.880
They’re making...

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.300
Yeah. This is...

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.010
Curry, right?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.430
Kawachi-san!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.770
Why are you here again?!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:47.020
I had the all-important task of buying fruit
found all over the Miyazaki prefecture.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.310
Gofer.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:49.780
Yeah, a gofer.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.650
But, you know...

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.780
CMAP doesn’t seem to be doing anything special.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.360
Why do you say that?

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:59.280
It’s true that curry made of ripe mangoes
should be delicious with a deep flavor...

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.580
But, they’ll be using curry powder
for their primary flavor,

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:06.330
which is not even made in Miyazaki.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.720
What are you, an idiot?

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:11.540
You think they’re using curry powder
for their primary flavor?

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.540
Take another whiff of this fragrance.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.550
What is this?

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.050
It’s not just the fragrance of curry.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.050
It’s demiglace sauce!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.480
Exactly.

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:28.980
They’re probably using demiglace sauce
made from Miyazaki beef.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.060
Miyazaki beef?

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.400
If you put watery substances like the
curry you eat with rice into bread,

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.400
the bread will be completely soaked.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.570
That’s common sense.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.320
That’s why when you make curry bread,

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:44.570
you add in flour or bread crumbs to the curry
used for the filling to reduce the water content.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:48.670
After reducing the water content of the
demiglace sauce by simmering it for a long time,

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.970
they’ve mixed it with ripe mango curry.

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:55.170
This is what you do to create the
curry bread of the highest quality.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.670
B-But...

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:01.140
If you did that, wouldn’t the curry become less spicy?

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:04.430
It’s not like curry gets more delicious
with increased spiciness!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:08.100
What distinguishes good curry
from the bad is its flavor!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.600
And, look carefully.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.650
The technique that Narumi guy’s using...

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.870
It’s as though he’s painting a picture on water...

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:18.700
He’s mixing it slowly and gently.

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.370
That’s the movement of a person
who’s mastered western cooking!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.370
It’s known as “Tuning the Iron Pot”!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.910
While it may look simple,

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:31.120
that demiglace sauce has already been boiled down to as low as it can go.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:35.630
I’m sure you know how difficult it is to do that.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.920
H-How can that be?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.420
Is this CMAP’s...

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.680
Is this the true strength of
Japan’s best idol-cooking group?

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.400
It looks like you’ve finally figured it out.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.020
Wh-What’s with you?

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.610
The match is still on.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.770
This time, my job is sort of that of a commander’s.

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:59.070
With my having chosen all the ingredients
to be used in the match, my job is done.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.820
Oh, is that so?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.370
Then, it’s the same as my job, huh?

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:04.580
It’s completely different.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:06.080
Absolutely different.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.490
Oh?

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.120
It’s surprising that you are the commander.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.080
But then...

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.880
I’m sure that you already know
who the winner is going to be.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.260
In addition to Narumi...

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:22.840
the guy kneading the dough right now, Chimatsuri, is a highly talented individual, too.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:25.840
You guys don’t have any hope of winning.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.100
How stupid.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:32.770
No matter what talent you fellows may have,
you cannot win against Azuma.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:37.900
He has a natural gift that surpasses
even me, a genius of a commander.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.360
A genius of a commander?!

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.860
Oh? That guy has such a gift?

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.780
You’ll understand after you see him.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.240
Then, let me ask you this.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:51.870
Do you know that you shouldn’t add
fruit juice directly to bread dough?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.790
Of course I do!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:55.170
If you do something like that,

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:58.500
the proteases in the fruit juice will
digest the gluten of the dough,

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:01.130
and you won’t be able to knead it.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:04.300
Just like what happened to me in the newcomers’ battle,

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.640
when Yukino added endoproteases to my dough.

00:22:07.100 --> 00:22:10.930
When adding fruit juice to dough, you must boil it first.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.390
That’s common sense.

00:22:12.730 --> 00:22:14.730
Just as you’d expect of the commander.

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:15.390
However...

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:18.650
That guy... just added it to the dough.

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:21.400
Fruit juice that hasn’t been boiled at all, straight.

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:23.400
What was that?!

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:33.050
Oh, the dough’s all melted.

00:22:53.930 --> 00:23:02.230
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:10.280
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.050
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:19.040
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:26.630
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:43.400
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:51.990
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:02.540
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:08.550
Solar Hands are really not particularly great.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:10.560
Really kinda want him to die, right?

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.680
Let’s crush them into a fine pulp.

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:15.350
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.350 --> 00:24:17.060
Love will rescue Saito as well!!

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.850
The Solar Hands vs. The Flame Arm!

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:24.480
The really delicious and beautiful mango is considered to be

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:25.510
3 best fruits in the world
3 best fruits in the world

00:24:25.510 --> 00:24:27.730
one of the three best fruits in the world.

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:31.030
The other two are the mangosteen and the cherrymoya.

00:24:31.030 --> 00:24:31.740
That’s all.

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:34.500
Oh?!
